<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore non-oil exports fall 0.5 pct in December.</title>
<headline>Singapore non-oil exports fall 0.5 pct in December.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's non-oil domestic exports fell a nominal 0.5 percent year-on-year in December to Singapore $7.46 billion after falling 8.8 percent in November, the Trade Development Board (TDB) said on Monday.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of 15 financial institutions had predicted a nominal year-on-year rise of 2.9 percent in December.</p>
<p>In real terms, non-oil exports rose 4.6 percent in December to S$9.68 billion after falling 3.6 pct in November.  </p>
<p>Singapore's total trade growth for 1997 is expected to be between 5 to 7 percent, the TDB said.</p>
<p>The board said in a statement that the growth would probably be closer to the upper end of the range.  </p>
